>> title: Lo Mein
>> category: Noodles
>> tags: noodles, pork, cabbage, chinese, wok
>> counters: Takeout Counter
>> aka: lo mein, roast pork lo mein, lao mian, 撈麵, 捞面, soft noodles
>> pairs-with: char-siu, egg-rolls
>> servings: 4
>> time: 30 min
>> step.1: boil 3 min, drain, slick with oil
>> step.2: stir the sauce smooth
>> step.3: stir-fry the vegetables 3 min
>> step.4: warm the pork through 1 min
>> step.5: toss over high heat until it coats

Boil @fresh egg noodles{1%lb}(450 g; lo mein noodles) in a big #pot{} of unsalted water for ~boil{3%min}, drain them hard, and toss them with @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp} so they do not set into a block.

Stir @light soy sauce{2%Tbs}, @dark soy sauce{1%Tbs}, @oyster sauce{2%Tbs}, @chicken stock{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @sugar{1%tsp}, and @white pepper{1/4%tsp} together in a bowl.

Stir-fry @garlic{3%cloves}(minced) and @fresh ginger{1%Tbs}(grated) in @peanut oil{2%Tbs} in a hot #wok{}, then add @napa cabbage{3%cups}(225 g; shredded), @carrot{1%medium}(julienned), and @scallions{4}(cut in 2-in lengths) and cook ~stirfry{3%min}, until the cabbage is limp but still has a bite.

Add @char siu{8%oz}(225 g; sliced thin) to @&(~1)vegetables{} and ~stirfry{1%min} to warm it through.

Toss @&(~4)noodles{} and @&(~3)sauce{} into @&(~1)pork and vegetables{} over the highest heat the hob gives, lifting with tongs for ~stirfry{2%min} until every strand is brown and nothing pools in the pan.
